+profile (assumed): herdr-graph is a Rust Herdr plugin (Cargo `publish = false`, v0.2.0) that keeps a Git-backed organization graph for a single operator's coding-agent panes on one machine. Its only network surface is local Unix sockets to the Herdr host and its own daemon; there are no external users, no money, and no data beyond a local Git repo whose mutations are plan/confirm/apply with undo. Rollback is cheap (git, undoable plans, daemon restart). Blast radius is low: resilience and observability gaps cost the operator inconvenience, not data.
